{title: Heavenly Father Send Thy Blessing}
{artist: Christopher Wordsworth}
{key: Eb}
{time: 3/2}
{tempo: 120}

Verse 1
[Eb]Heav'nly Father, [Ab]send Thy [Eb]blessing On Thy [Fm]children [Fm7]ga[Bb]thered [Eb]here,
May they all, Thy [Ab]Name con[Eb]fessing, Be to [Fm]Thee fo[Fm7]re[Bb]ver [Eb]dear;
May they be, like [Ab]Joseph, [Eb]loving, Dutiful, and [Ab]chaste, and [Eb]pure;
And their faith, like [Ab]David, [Eb]proving, Steadfast [Fm]unto [Fm7]death [Bb]en[Eb]dure.

Verse 2
[Eb]Holy Savior, [Ab]who in [Eb]meekness Didst vouch[Fm]safe a [Fm7]child [Bb]to [Eb]be,
Guide their steps, and [Ab]help their [Eb]weakness, Bless and [Fm]make them [Fm7]like [Bb]to [Eb]Thee;
Bear Thy lambs, when [Ab]they are [Eb]weary, In Thine arms and [Ab]at Thy [Eb]breast;
Through life's desert, [Ab]dry and [Eb]dreary, Bring them [Fm]to Thy [Fm7]heav'n[Bb]ly [Eb]rest.

Verse 3
[Eb]Spread Thy golden [Ab]pinions [Eb]o'er them, Holy [Fm]Spirit, [Fm7]from [Bb]a[Eb]bove,
Guide them, lead them, [Ab]go be[Eb]fore them, Give them [Fm]peace, and [Fm7]joy, [Bb]and [Eb]love;
Thy true temples, [Ab]Holy [Eb]Spirit, May they with Thy [Ab]glory [Eb]shine,
And immortal [Ab]bliss in[Eb]herit, And for [Fm]ever[Fm7]more [Bb]be [Eb]Thine.
